# Reference UI Parity (Mandatory)

When the user shares **screenshots**, **Figma links**, **ClickUp UI references**, or says **"match web UI"**, **"exact like SS"**, **"same as reference"**, or similar:

## Source of truth

1. The reference is the **contract** — not generic SaaS patterns, not Linear/Vercel/Notion defaults.
2. **Parity beats creativity.** Do not redesign, "premium-ify", or simplify unless the user explicitly asks.
3. If reference conflicts with `premium-saas.mdc`, **reference wins**.

## Before writing code

Complete a **Reference Parity Inventory** (mental or written). For each screenshot, list every visible element:

| Area | Capture |
|------|---------|
| Page shell | Title, subtitle, actions (refresh, create, etc.), footer |
| Navigation | Primary tabs (active/inactive styles), secondary tabs, icons |
| Section headers | Title + subtitle + header actions on same row rules |
| Filters | Search placeholder, dropdown labels, inline vs stacked layout |
| Cards / panels | Title-only vs title+subtitle, borders, padding, embedded tables |
| Tables | Column headers (case, size, color), row cells, badges, chips, actions |
| Badges & chips | Filled vs outline, color, radius, label casing |
| Typography | Weights, sizes, muted vs primary text |
| Spacing | Gaps between sections, row padding, alignment (left/center/right) |
| States | Empty, loading, error — only if shown in reference |
| Mock data | Names, URLs, counts, dates, status labels visible in SS |

Do not start implementation until the inventory is complete.

## Reuse first (this repo)

Before creating new UI primitives, search and reuse patterns from completed modules:

| Pattern | Look in |
|---------|---------|
| Pill tabs (primary + secondary) | `ConfigurationPrimaryTabs`, `ConfigurationSecondaryTabs`, `CrawlSegmentTabs` |
| Section / panel cards | `ConfigurationPanelCard`, `CrawlPanelCard` |
| Screen layout + breakpoints | `configuration-layout.ts`, `crawl-layout.ts`, `use*Layout` hooks |
| Filter row (search + selects) | `CrawlMobileFilterSection`, `CrawlSearchField`, `CrawlFilterSelect` |
| Table + header rows | `CrawlSourcesTable`, `CrawlSourcesTableHeader`, `ApiKeyTableRow` |
| Status badges | `CrawlStatusBadge` |
| Sheets / modals | `ConfigurationSheet`, crawl overlay sheets |
| Theme-driven styling | `useAppTheme`, shared `app-*-field` components |

Extend existing components. Do not parallel-implement the same pattern under a new name.

Full shared component catalog: [docs/CODE_CONVENTIONS.md](../../docs/CODE_CONVENTIONS.md). Module layout context: [docs/PRODUCT.md](../../docs/PRODUCT.md).

## Implementation rules

- Match **layout hierarchy** first (what is outside cards vs inside, what shares a row).
- Match **inactive tab text color** (usually `colors.text`, not `textMuted`) and **active filled primary**.
- Match **border radius** per element type (tabs `radius.sm`, badges often `radius.lg` pill).
- Match **label casing** exactly (`Active`, `ONCE`, `Idle`, `Ready`, uppercase table headers).
- Match **column structure** and **horizontal alignment** (identity left, metrics right, chevron far right).
- Use **theme tokens** (`colors`, `spacing`, `typography`, `radius`) — never hardcode unless reference shows a fixed semantic color (e.g. success green `#15803d`).
- Preserve **mobile card fallbacks** at compact breakpoints; web table layout at wide breakpoints.

## After implementation

Run a **Parity Checklist** — every inventory item must be PASS or explicitly noted as blocked:

```md
Reference Parity Checklist
- [ ] Page header (title, subtitle, actions)
- [ ] Primary tabs (style, active state, icons)
- [ ] Section header (title, subtitle, actions row)
- [ ] Secondary tabs
- [ ] Filters (placeholders, count, layout)
- [ ] Panel card structure
- [ ] Table/list columns and alignment
- [ ] Badges, chips, status colors
- [ ] Typography weights and sizes
- [ ] Spacing and borders
- [ ] Mock/sample data matches reference
- [ ] Responsive behavior at key breakpoints (1280, 900, 720, mobile)
```

Do **not** claim complete until the checklist is done or the user accepts known gaps.

## When user says "exact" or shares SS again

- Treat feedback as **missed parity**, not a style preference.
- Re-read the screenshot element-by-element; fix the specific drift (tabs, alignment, badge shape, etc.).
- Do not respond with generic improvements — fix the delta.

